From: NWA50BE OpenWrt Project <noreply@invalid.example>
Subject: [PATCH] ipq53xx: backport kernel network fixes to 6.6.88
SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-2.0-only

The ipq53xx kernel stays at 6.6.88 and gets no 6.6.y updates. Add:

  0964, 0965  TIP's own backports from v5.2.0-rc1 (bd829c10): nf_tables
              use-after-free in nf_tables_addchain() (CVE-2026-23231) and
              the posix-cpu-timers race (CVE-2025-38352, CISA KEV; not
              reachable with POSIX_CPU_TIMERS_TASK_WORK=y)
  901-908     CVE-2026-99288: a SYN flood to a listening port can make
              the established-socket lookup pick up a socket that is not
              hashed yet and dereference a NULL rsk_listener; with
              PANIC_ON_OOPS=y that reboots the AP from the LAN. 908 is
              the fix (6.6.y cedc85d95ce0, refreshed for offsets only);
              901, 902 and 907 are the earlier 6.6.y fixes its TCP Fast
              Open and request-timer hunks build on (CVE-2025-39955,
              CVE-2025-40186, CVE-2026-99270)
  903         CVE-2026-98255: old ACKs no longer advance the window on
              the TCP fast path (RFC 5961 check)
  904         CVE-2026-98532: ipv6_find_hdr() cannot return an offset
              past the packet
  905, 906    CVE-2026-99077, CVE-2026-99076: UDP PMTU and redirect
              exceptions are created before socket matching, so the
              result no longer depends on whether a socket matched
  909         CVE-2026-99805: bounded VLAN-0 tag stripping

All are linux-6.6.y stable commits with their headers kept. In
patch-kernel.sh order they apply on 6.6.88 with TIP's 934 patches and
900 (0046) at fuzz 0; none touches a file another patch here changes.

